<text>target = gen_symlink_name(depth, profile->rawdata->name, name);</text>
Reason:
The function `rawdata_get_link_base` accesses `profile->rawdata->name` without first checking whether `profile->rawdata` is NULL. When the `aa_g_export_binary` parameter is disabled at runtime and a profile is replaced, the `rawdata` pointer is set to NULL, causing a NULL pointer dereference (oops).

The code statements that fix the bug are:
<text>if (!profile->rawdata) {
    aa_put_label(label);
    return ERR_PTR(-ENOENT);
}</text>
Reason:
The fix adds a NULL check for `profile->rawdata` before any dereference occurs. If `rawdata` is NULL, the function returns `-ENOENT` (no such file or directory), preventing the NULL pointer dereference. The acquired label reference is properly released before returning.

